    "summary": "On 27 March 2019 ACM named Yoshua Bengio, Geoffrey Hinton and Yann LeCun recipients of the 2018 A.M. Turing Award for conceptual and engineering breakthroughs that have made deep neural networks an important component of computing. The announcement says that, working independently and together, the three developed conceptual foundations for the field, identified surprising phenomena through experiments, and contributed engineering advances, and it links their work to progress in computer vision, speech recognition and natural language processing. In 2021 the three gave a Turing Lecture on deep learning that was published in Communications of the ACM.",
